# Milestone: M3
# Covers: nested tag-scope + try/finally cleanup ordering per row 7 §6.3;
#         verifies that the unwind walker pops TAG_SCOPE entries in innermost-
#         first order through nested scopes, executing each onleave body before
#         continuing outward.
#
# blocked: requires string concat (T46 dropped) + & separator hangs chk driver
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason: requires onleave clause parse/emit (M5 reactive runtime).  At M3,
# the row 7 unwind walker handles TAG_SCOPE absorption (pop-and-continue for
# normal exit) but there is no parse support for the `onleave` keyword so
# no onleave body can be installed.  The nested try/finally ordering is
# already tested by tests/chk/control_transfer/nested_finally.chk; the
# full tag-scope + try/finally combination must wait for M5.
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: log records cleanup in innermost-first order "ioIO".
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5):
#   var log = "";
#   var outer = Tag.new;
#   var inner = Tag.new;
#   try {
#     outer: {
#       try {
#         inner: { outer.stop() }
#           onleave { log = log + "i" }
#       } finally { log = log + "I" }
#     } onleave { log = log + "o" }
#   } finally { log = log + "O" };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "ioIO"
